############ HOW TO READ IT ############
  [CUDA memcpy HtoD] on the host arm should be ~= the logical dataset
  size (the connector re-uploading what the app just downloaded). On the
  device arm the input HtoD should be ~0. That delta is the overhead a
  filter cannot avoid, because H5Z only ever sees host bytes.

  If BOTH arms show the same HtoD, the VOL is not honouring the device
  pointer -- it is staging through host memory internally. Fix the
  connector, not the plot.

  CHUNKING: this ran with VOL_COMP_CHUNKING=none. The rest of the
  figure uses VOL config 'native' for every dataset except qmc, which
  uses vol_N8. If 'none' is not the same geometry, the device bar is
  not comparable to the bars beside it -- rerun with the matching value.

